🛡️ Windows Fundamentals for SOC Analysts
Track: SOC Analyst Foundations
Focus: Windows internals, endpoint telemetry, and investigation fundamentals

Detailed study report focused only on the Windows concepts required to build a strong SOC foundation
🎯 Scope: Windows architecture, processes & services, users & permissions, file system, registry, PowerShell, and Windows
Security. The report deliberately excludes unrelated Windows administration and end-user topics.
🧭 How to use this report: Study each section, reproduce the hands-on commands in a Windows VM, and connect every
concept to the question: “What evidence would a SOC analyst see if an attacker abused this component?”

📌 1. What You Actually Need to Learn
Area	SOC Objective	Priority
Windows architecture	Understand major components and where security telemetry originates.	High
Processes & services	Identify suspicious execution, parent-child relationships, persistence, and service abuse.	Very High
Users & permissions	Understand identities, groups, privileges, UAC, and access control.	Very High
File system	Understand NTFS, permissions, paths, metadata, and attacker-abused locations.	High
Registry	Understand configuration, persistence, execution, and investigation locations.	Very High
