📌 9. Hands-On Windows Lab
Use a Windows virtual machine for practice. Do not perform security testing on systems you do not own or have explicit
permission to test.
Lab 1 — Process Investigation
- Open Task Manager and identify running processes.
- Use PowerShell to list processes and sort by CPU or memory.
- Pick a legitimate process and inspect its executable path and account.
- Use Sysinternals Process Explorer later to compare what additional process information is available.
Get-Process | Sort-Object CPU -Descending | Select-Object -First 10
Lab 2 — Users and Privileges
whoami /all
Get-LocalUser
Get-LocalGroupMember Administrators
- Identify your current user, groups and privileges.
- Understand which account is privileged and why.
  Lab 3 — File Investigation
Get-ChildItem $env:TEMP
Get-FileHash "$env:WINDIR\System32\notepad.exe" -Algorithm SHA256
Get-Acl "$env:WINDIR\System32\notepad.exe"
Lab 4 — Registry
reg query HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
- Document what startup entries exist on your lab machine.
  Lab 5 — Event Viewer
- Open Event Viewer.
- Navigate to Windows Logs → Security.
- Find a successful logon (4624) and failed logon (4625) if available.
- Record timestamp, account, logon type and source information where present.
  Lab 6 — PowerShell Telemetry
- Run harmless PowerShell commands and observe what appears in PowerShell logs when logging is enabled.
- Learn to distinguish command content, process information and authentication context.
📌 10. SOC Investigation Thinking
For every Windows alert, train yourself to answer these questions:
- Who — which account or security principal performed the action?
- What — what process, command, file, service or registry value was involved?
- Where — on which host and from which path/source did it occur?
- When — exact timestamp and sequence of events?
- How — parent process, command line, authentication method or execution mechanism?
- Why — is there a legitimate business explanation?
- What next — what additional telemetry should be checked?
